A stop of a thread another core runs shoots that core but does not mark its trap,
so the trap goes on as the thread's if a call between resumed it, a call made on registers a watcher may have written:
a core whose turn another core stopped drops the trap it takes next.

Caught-by: fuzz-smp2
Report: a core would take a trap as the thread another core stopped
Witness: fuzz-smp2 cores-resume-before-trap

